The post-release commit only allows `^lib/.*\.pm$` (the @Git::VersionManager default) plus the bundle's `^bin/` (GETTY.pm, `post-release commit.allow_dirty_match`). A dist that installs its program from another directory via `[ExecDir] dir = script` gets that file into :PerlExecFiles, so BumpVersionAfterRelease rewrites its $VERSION, but the post-release Git::Commit does not commit it: the bump stays as an uncommitted change, history falls one version behind, and the next release trips over the dirty tree. `commit_files_after_release` feeds only the pre-tag release commit, and the bundle has no config slicing, so a dist cannot fix it in dist.ini.

Found in briefing (App-Briefing 0.006000, briefing card k41): its bin/ belongs to the Claude Code plugin, so the CPAN program lives in script/ with [ExecDir] dir = script.

Possible fix: derive the extra allow_dirty_match from the ExecDir directory (or also allow `^script/`). Maintainer wants this fixed and released before the App-Briefing release.

